Foundational proposition: Transform articulated substrate values into verifiable technological behaviors through distributed consensus, epistemic governance, cryptographic integrity, and bounded autonomous execution.

The concept introduces a distinction between what a system values, how those values are represented, and how participating technologies collectively verify and enforce them.

Rather than treating Byzantine consensus exclusively as agreement about transaction ordering or network state, Conceptual Byzantine Behavioral Consensus extends the conceptual model to agreement about authorized behavior, evidence quality, operational constraints, and integrity conditions.

